# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for this Next.js 14 project following the latest official documentation from Vercel.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- **Installed**: `@vercel/analytics` version `^2.0.1`
- **Package Manager**: npm
- **Command used**: `npm install @vercel/analytics`

### 2. Configuration
**Modified**: `frontend/src/app/layout.tsx`
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component to the root layout, placed after `</ThemeProvider>` and before `</body>`
- This follows the Next.js App Router pattern as specified in the official Vercel documentation

### 3. Files Modified
- `frontend/package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `frontend/package-lock.json` - Updated with new package dependencies
- `frontend/src/app/layout.tsx` - Configured Analytics component

## Implementation Details

The Analytics component was added according to the official Vercel documentation for Next.js App Router:
- Import from `@vercel/analytics/next` (framework-specific import)
- Placed in the root layout file at `src/app/layout.tsx`
- Positioned at the end of the `<body>` tag to ensure proper page load performance

## Verification

✅ Package successfully installed in node_modules
✅ No linting errors introduced by our changes (ran `npx next lint --file src/app/layout.tsx`)
✅ TypeScript types are correct (Analytics component is properly typed)
✅ Lock file updated to ensure consistent dependency resolution

## Pre-existing Issues

Note: The project had pre-existing linting errors in other files:
- `src/app/dashboard/backtest/page.tsx` (unused imports)
- `src/components/chart/candlestick-chart.tsx` (unused variable)

These were not introduced by this change and were not addressed as they are outside the scope of this task.

## Next Steps for Deployment

To enable Web Analytics on Vercel:
1. Deploy this code to Vercel
2. Navigate to your project dashboard on Vercel
3. Go to the "Analytics" tab
4. Enable Web Analytics
5. Once enabled, analytics will automatically start tracking page views

The Analytics component will only send data when deployed on Vercel. In local development, it will not send any data.
